        "title": "Trump administration deported US citizen to Mexico, DoJ admits in court",
        "source": "The Guardian - World news",
        "source_id": "guardian_world",
        "category": "news",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/nov/23/trump-administration-deported-citizen-mexico",
        "published_at": "2026-11-23T11:00:56",
        "level": "C2",
        "slot_level": "C2",
        "source_level": "C2",
        "word_count": 619,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "The Trump administration recently admitted in federal court that it deported a US citizen to Mexico after American authorities incorrectly concluded he was an undocumented immigrant.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "a9e8d0140a0927d59c764603863401f74cd68859",
        "summary": "Brian Morales García of Texas seeks damages after he was wrongly identified as undocumented in case White House wants dropped The Trump administration recently admitted in federal court that it deported a US citizen to Mexico after American authorities incorrectly concluded he was an undocumented immigrant. Attorneys for the US justice department made that admission on Friday while requesting the dismissal of a lawsuit for damages that the deported man – Brian José Morales García of Austin, Texas – has been pursuing against the federal government.",
