        "id": 45,
        "title": "Weird lifestyle advice from Gwyneth Paltrow: best podcasts of the week",
        "source": "The Guardian - Culture",
        "source_id": "guardian_culture",
        "category": "culture",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2026/nov/23/weird-lifestyle-advice-from-gwyneth-paltrow-best-podcasts-of-the-week",
        "published_at": "2026-11-23T07:00:49",
        "level": "C2",
        "slot_level": "C2",
        "source_level": "C2",
        "word_count": 362,
        "duration_sec": null,
        "body_text": "Pick of the week The Goop Guide With Gwyneth Paltrow The second podcast from her wellness empire is ostensibly centred on Paltrow’s incredibly niche lifestyle advice: where to eat the “best cacio e pepe in Rome”, for example, or “whether it’s weird to use an obsidian gua sha tool on a plane”.",
        "audio_url": null,
        "description": null,
        "license": "proprietary",
        "attribution": null,
        "truncated": true,
        "guid_hash": "571f7f985782ce038fbdfe2f36129b5e7776b247",
        "summary": "The Hollywood star is joined by celebrity guests as she shares ‘practical tips’. Plus, David Cameron’s deeply personal series about Alzheimer’s The second podcast from her wellness empire is ostensibly centred on Paltrow’s incredibly niche lifestyle advice: where to eat the “best cacio e pepe in Rome”, for example, or “whether it’s weird to use an obsidian gua sha tool on a plane”. In reality, the show is a weekly cosy chat with a showbiz pal (first up, Zoe Saldaña) peppered with a few practical tips – such as how to eat enough protein if you can’t face any more eggs. Rachel Aroesti Widely available, episodes weekly",
        "origin": "fresh",
        "badges": [],
        "periods": [],
